<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 2) (Ovis ammon (Argali): real skull photograph + Thompson's Fig. 320; Capra sinaitica: Thompson's Fig. 319)",
        "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Ovis ammon (Argali): real skull photograph + Thompson's Fig. 320; Capra sinaitica: Thompson's Fig. 319 morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-031-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-031-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-031-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-031-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-031-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-031_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks-with-a.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ovis ammon (Argali): real skull photograph + Thompson's Fig. 320; Capra sinaitica: Thompson's Fig. 319 specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-031_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks-with-a.py> ;
    schema:about "Ovis ammon (Argali): real skull photograph + Thompson's Fig. 320; Capra sinaitica: Thompson's Fig. 319" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: torsion / St Venant warping; inter-species beta differences; thickness-curvature rule; teeth or tusks",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E1 free-pole log-spiral fits of the outer edge of Fig. 320, Fig. 319 and the Argali photograph; AIC vs Archimedean spiral and circle; bootstrap CI; KS test",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E4 ray-based breadth test about the fitted pole; E2 implied cone semi-angle; sensitivity sectors; synthetic controls and ablation",
        "reported_in_source: Argali species share alpha but differ in the cone/helical component beta (pp. 617-618)",
        "reported_in_source: Ovis ammon spiral angle about 75 deg; Highland ram a little more; Scinde wild goat < 70 deg; Oryx 20-40 deg (p. 617)",
        "reported_in_source: trihedral edge lengths 80:74:45 cm (p. 618); St Venant torsion curves on the rings (pp. 621-624)",
        "transfer_boundary: a lateral 2D projection measures k_proj = sin(beta) cot(alpha), not alpha itself",
        "transfer_boundary: the Argali photograph is perspective, not orthographic; the flaring tip arc drives the spiral estimate (sensitivity flag)" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-031_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks-with-a.py; output: docs/media/t1917_031_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_comparison.png; organism: Ovis ammon (Argali): real skull photograph + Thompson's Fig. 320; Capra sinaitica: Thompson's Fig. 319; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Ovis ammon spiral angle about 75 deg; Highland ram a little more; Scinde wild goat < 70 deg; Oryx 20-40 deg (p. 617) | Argali species share alpha but differ in the cone/helical component beta (pp. 617-618) | trihedral edge lengths 80:74:45 cm (p. 618); St Venant torsion curves on the rings (pp. 621-624); reconstructed_in_script: E1 free-pole log-spiral fits of the outer edge of Fig. 320, Fig. 319 and the Argali photograph; AIC vs Archimedean spiral and circle; bootstrap CI; KS test | E4 ray-based breadth test about the fitted pole; E2 implied cone semi-angle; sensitivity sectors; synthetic controls and ablation; transfer_boundary: a lateral 2D projection measures k_proj = sin(beta) cot(alpha), not alpha itself | the Argali photograph is perspective, not orthographic; the flaring tip arc drives the spiral estimate (sensitivity flag); does_not_claim: torsion / St Venant warping; inter-species beta differences; thickness-curvature rule; teeth or tusks]; other sources: On Growth and Form — Ch. XIII, The Shapes of Horns, and of Teeth or Tusks: with a Note on Torsion <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>; phenomenon_size: 948 µm (0.000948 m, log10=-3.023 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 948 µm to 2.89 m): 948 µm:ovis-aries-bioelectric-polarity, 3.5 mm:ovis-aries-vertex-packing, 6.4 cm:ovis-aries-turing-wavelength, 12.0 cm:ovis-aries-clock-wavefront, 19.4 cm:ovis-aries-morphogen-condensation, 28.4 cm:ovis-aries-elastic-buckling, 48.0 cm:ovis-aries-flux-canalization, 63.5 cm:ovis-aries-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/s002850050081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/s12915-021-00990-w>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.qz612jmb4> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-model-fidelity>,
