<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 2) — Code-to-model traceability: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Docstring maps E1-E5 and tests T1-T4 to pages; every fit/segmentation step is a named function with its equation id; reference.json carries the loci; the math-KG YAML links five laws to Lean declarations and script line ranges. Deductions: the ray-based inner-edge rule and the trimming rule are the script's own constructions, not Thompson's whorl-breadth procedure (Ch. XI p. 558), and this is only stated in comments." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 2) — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "E1-E4 implemented as Thompson states them; E2 is now used in the right direction (implied beta from k_proj rather than treating alpha_proj as alpha), and the Lean module proves the non-identifiability that this rests on plus the Pass-2 data pins (alpha match, dAIC, E4 failure) with 0 sorry. The gnomonic test implements E4 literally (breadth along rays). Still 2D: no 3D centreline, so beta is inferred, never measured; E5 remains a rendering." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/result.json (generated output, not in repo): beta_implied_deg reported, not measured; cone component untested — datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/result.json: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-031_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks-with-a.py at 430ab132, application/json, 6709 B, artifact_sha256 b497cdf5262491b910f2627c5070cf6117f86f2ec7fade66cf8a1d33ff98edc4 (sha256 b497cdf5262491b910f2627c5070cf6117f86f2ec7fade66cf8a1d33ff98edc4), spec_fingerprint 860e7e35af4127f92fad446ceb9389d004fdb7dfa2fe98cf3f8ad3f9657429c2" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 2) — Morphometric validation: 66/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Per source: alpha_proj with bootstrap 95 % CI, R, Pearson r, RMSE (abs and relative), KS p-value, dAIC vs two nulls, implied beta, k_breadth vs k_outer; plus positive/negative controls, a shuffled ablation, sector-sensitivity ranges and a species contrast — 23 measurement rows with reference values. Deductions: the bootstrap CI (+/-0.5 deg) understates the model uncertainty revealed by the sector sensitivity (up to 12 deg); the gnomonic test is pole-dependent and inconclusive on the photo; the KS test rejects normality on Fig. 320 (ring corrugations); n = 1 real specimen." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/result.json (generated output, not in repo): sector_sensitivity flags true for the photo and the Capra figure — datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/result.json: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-031_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks-with-a.py at 430ab132, application/json, 6709 B, artifact_sha256 b497cdf5262491b910f2627c5070cf6117f86f2ec7fade66cf8a1d33ff98edc4 (sha256 b497cdf5262491b910f2627c5070cf6117f86f2ec7fade66cf8a1d33ff98edc4), spec_fingerprint 860e7e35af4127f92fad446ceb9389d004fdb7dfa2fe98cf3f8ad3f9657429c2" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-measurement-ablation-fig-320-radii-shuffled-against-angles-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-measurement-argali-specimen-photo-delta-aic-archimedean-minus-log-spiral>,
