<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 67.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Fig. 320 (Ovis ammon drawing, 521 pts, 269 deg): alpha_proj 84.2 deg [83.7, 84.6], R 1.90, r 0.968, RMSE 3.7 %, log spiral beats circle by dAIC 425 and Archimedean by 22; beta implied by alpha = 75 deg is 22 deg. Real Argali horn (HSV sheath mask, 478 pts, 215 deg): alpha_proj 74.7 deg [73.6, 75.6], R 5.57, r 0.995, RMSE 2.6 %, dAIC circle 666, Archimedean +2 — matches Thompson's 75 deg, but dropping the ventral/tip arc makes the remaining arc circle-like (sensitivity range 74.7-87.0 deg). Capra sinaitica half-whorl: alpha not identifiable (53-86 deg across sectors). Gnomonic test fails on Fig. 320 (|k_breadth| 0.32 vs |k_outer| 0.13), inconclusive on the photo. Controls: synthetic alpha 75 recovered to 75.0, circle null -> circle, shuffled ablation r 0.97 -> 0.01. Verdict mixed. Overall 67.6/100. Overall 67.6/100 (faithfulness 65.4, reproducibility 72.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 430ab132; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 58, Parameter expressivity 70, Morphometric validation 66, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 74, Reproducibility package 64. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_031_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-031_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks-with-a.py at 430ab132, image/png, 971711 B, 2000×1300 px, artifact_sha256 832658753c97c6a0b4a0515850d6da3c331ef1486eba4eb5122a83df35453fd5 (sha256 832658753c97c6a0b4a0515850d6da3c331ef1486eba4eb5122a83df35453fd5), spec_fingerprint 860e7e35af4127f92fad446ceb9389d004fdb7dfa2fe98cf3f8ad3f9657429c2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 860e7e35af4127f92fad446ceb9389d004fdb7dfa2fe98cf3f8ad3f9657429c2; artifact_sha256: 832658753c97c6a0b4a0515850d6da3c331ef1486eba4eb5122a83df35453fd5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/dryad_qz612jmb4_dataset_Tidiereetal2020.txt=8e13941af7964f2d..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/ovis_ammon_argali_skull_horns_specimen.jpg=f8c17c09c7ebe13e..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/paper_citations.bib=eb8c1ca49ca4877d..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/scout_manifest.json=c6e9d7fbfcf1ea70..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/t1917_031_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_reference.json=0395050a08978a58..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/thompson_1917_fig318_ram_horns_diagram.jpg=18f820edfb2de26c..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/thompson_1917_fig319_capra_sinaitica_head.jpg=55131cbad1f81417..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/thompson_1917_fig320_ovis_ammon_head.jpg=4d6a6093ce49a70a...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-031-the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-tee-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Ovis ammon spiral angle about 75 deg; Highland ram a little more; Scinde wild goat < 70 deg; Oryx 20-40 deg (p. 617) | Argali species share alpha but differ in the cone/helical component beta (pp. 617-618) | trihedral edge lengths 80:74:45 cm (p. 618); St Venant torsion curves on the rings (pp. 621-624); reconstructed_in_script: E1 free-pole log-spiral fits of the outer edge of Fig. 320, Fig. 319 and the Argali photograph; AIC vs Archimedean spiral and circle; bootstrap CI; KS test | E4 ray-based breadth test about the fitted pole; E2 implied cone semi-angle; sensitivity sectors; synthetic controls and ablation; transfer_boundary: a lateral 2D projection measures k_proj = sin(beta) cot(alpha), not alpha itself | the Argali photograph is perspective, not orthographic; the flaring tip arc drives the spiral estimate (sensitivity flag); does_not_claim: torsion / St Venant warping; inter-species beta differences; thickness-curvature rule; teeth or tusks." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) — still builder-scored'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R10', 'item': 'Replace the ray-based breadth test with a pole-free local test (breadth vs radius of curvature along the outer edge)'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R11', 'item': 'Fit the Capra sinaitica horn only with a constrained pole (e.g. on the horn-base normal) or use a full-whorl Capra falconeri specimen so the goat-vs-sheep contrast is identifiable'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R8', 'item': '3D centrelines (MorphoSource CT or photogrammetry) for >= 3 Argali / Ovis specimens to measure alpha and beta separately and test the cone/torsion component'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R9', 'item': 'Orthographic lateral photographs of isolated horn sheaths (museum specimens) so the sector-sensitivity of alpha_proj disappears and the breadth test becomes conclusive'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 6.76e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

