    dct:description "A real Ovis ammon horn is now segmented (HSV sheath mask excludes the bleached skull) and the fitted spiral tracks its outer edge over 215 deg with 2.6 % RMSE; the overlay on Thompson's Fig. 320 tracks the dorsal/posterior edge; the E2 helicoid is rendered with the Fig.-320-implied beta. Deductions: n = 1 real specimen in perspective view, the spiral estimate on it is driven by the tip arc (sensitivity flag), the Capra figure is a halftone whose half-whorl cannot pin alpha, and the visual match of the helicoid to the photograph is qualitative." ;
